* The hidden water channel under the bottom-left caves (openc2e Creatures 2
* project, our own script; owner, 2026-11-11: a norn kept falling into it and
* could not get out). Run by openc2e after the world loads (Additions
* folder); safe to repeat.
*
* East of the cave with the gold vase (room 100, x 1450-2206) the picture is
* solid rock, but the room map goes on: rooms 94 and 96 (x 2206-2800, floor
* y 2320) lie inside the rock over a water channel (room 95, water, y
* 2320-2399), and their floor is the water's surface, so a creature that
* walked east out of the cave walked into the wall and dropped into the
* water. The channel's doors out were closed to creatures (room 206 behind
* the waterwheel, size 100; the cave, 0), so it stayed.
* - The way down into the channel from the cave (100 to 95) is closed.
*   (Opening the channel onto the cave with a ramp let creatures out, but
*   also let cave walkers slide in.)
* - Room 94 (x 2206-2308) is not rock: it is the bottom of lift 3 2 3's
*   shaft, whose lowest stop (call button at 2143,2221) is at the cave's
*   floor, and the cave's only way out but for the far west end of the
*   bottom tunnel, which is closed. Closing 100 to 94 here (2026-11-11)
*   sealed the cave and the whole tunnel (rooms 100, 101, 104, 105), and
*   a grendel starved there (7YZS, 2026-11-12). So the cave opens onto the
*   lift's stop again (100 to 94). The stop's side into the rock room over
*   the channel (94 to 96, the way creatures fell in) was closed until
*   2026-11-14, when it became the ramp into the stream (below). The stop's
*   own floor holds: its doorway down into the water (94 to 95, size 100)
*   is too small for creatures.
* - Creatures in the channel, the rock room over it or the pit behind the
*   waterwheel are carried off by the stream (below).
setv door 0 100 94 255
setv door 0 100 95 0
*
* The ramp (owner, 2026-11-14: "rather than a dock ... a ramp down into
* that water where creatures can wade ... they'll continue forward until
* the waterwheel sucks them out and spits them into a broader area"). The
* dock stays flat under the lift's bottom stop (x 2220-2324), so riders
* still step out dry; past its east end planks run down into the stream at
* about 17 degrees and into the earth of its bed (sprite zcrp: the dock's own
* boards and log laid along the slope by
* art/cave_ramp.py from the player's own dock and stream). Room
* 96, the air over the channel, now reaches down to the bed (y 2399) with
* its floor along the planks: 2320 to where they start (x 2332), 2384 at
* x 2545, then along the bed to x 2800. The water room (95) keeps only the
* part under the dock (x 2206-2308), out of reach. The way from the lift's
* stop onto the ramp (94 to 96) is open, so a creature walking east does
* not stop at the dock's end; past x 2330 the stream (below) takes it down
* the planks, along the bed beneath the wheel and up onto the ledge at its top.
* The cave and its tunnel (rooms 100-105) had only the lift as a way out.
room 95 2206 2320 2308 2399 room 95 4 room 95 5 room 95 6 room 95 7 room 95 8 room 95 9 room 95 12 room 95 13 room 95 14 room 95 15 room 95 16 room 95 17 room 95 19
room 96 2308 2180 2800 2399 room 96 4 room 96 5 room 96 6 room 96 7 room 96 8 room 96 9 room 96 12 room 96 13 room 96 14 room 96 15 room 96 16 room 96 17 room 96 19
* (the floor keeps the dock's height to x 2332, where the planks start, then
* follows them: creatures stand as far above them as on the dock's boards;
* owner, 2026-11-14, "a few pixels lower than where it looks like they
* should be")
ssfc 96 4 0 79 24 79 237 15 492 15
setv door 0 94 96 255
setv door 0 95 96 0
* (and room 95's old doorway to the pit behind the waterwheel, room 206,
* x 2800-3060: room 95 now ends at x 2308, 500 px short of it, so the
* doorway joins rooms that do not touch; no creature or object could use
* it, but food smell spread through it as if they did; 2026-11-16)
setv door 0 95 206 0
enum 2 3 252 doif posl eq 2300 kill targ endi next
enum 2 3 222 kill targ next
inst new: simp zcrp 1 0 -5 0 setv cls2 2 3 222 setv attr 0 mvto 2300 2290 slow
* The stream bed's earth in front of creatures, down past the foot of the
* world's picture (sprite zsbd, by art/stream_bed.py from the
* player's own earth; owner, 2026-11-14: creatures carried along the bed
* poked out below the ground). Class 2 3 221 (until 2026-11-14 night
* 2 3 251, which the volcano passage's picture uses: this file then removed
* it; the plank ramp likewise moved from 2 3 252 to 2 3 222). Plane 8002, in front of creatures and the
* wheel's foot, x 2200-3080 from just under the water.
enum 2 3 251 doif posl eq 2200 kill targ endi next
enum 2 3 221 kill targ next
inst new: simp zsbd 1 0 8002 0 setv cls2 2 3 221 setv attr 0 mvto 2200 2340 slow
*
* The stream (owner, 2026-11-13: a norn stuck in the little cave with a pool
* by the waterwheel, part of room 96; "if a norn is on the west side of the
* waterwheel, it should get swept beneath it and out toward the east").
* Creatures still get in: the lift's cabin (x 2220-2324) is wider than its
* shaft's room (94, to x 2308), so a rider in its east side came down over
* room 96, whose floor is the water's surface, and dropped into the channel;
* and the pit behind the waterwheel (room 206, x 2800-3060, every doorway 100
* or 0) is as closed. A watcher (2 1 156, invisible, every 2 s) finds a
* creature there (in the water, or wholly east of the lift's shaft, so riders
* are left alone) and carries it east along the channel's bed beneath the
* wheel (which is drawn in front of creatures), round its rim, and sets it
* down on the rock ledge at the wheel's top where the walkway over the mist
* starts (room 97, x about 2895, floor y 2150; until 2026-11-14 it was
* thrown on over the bridge to the garden's floor, x 3380). Each creature caught gets a
* carrier of its own (2 1 158), so several are carried at once. Moved by script all the way, so the landing
* does not count as a fall the creature should learn from.
*
* Objects too (owner, 2026-11-13: about 25 hungry creatures crowded the
* lift's shaft). Food and toys dropped by riders fell into the channel and
* piled up just past the shaft's east wall (x 2309, on the channel's bed);
* creatures at the foot of the shaft saw food 40 px away and walked into
* that wall for it again and again. Carryable objects (attr 1) in the
* channel, the rock room over it or the pit are set down on the cave's
* floor west of the shaft (room 100, floor y 2320), where they can be
* reached.
enum 2 1 156 kill targ next
inst new: simp blnk 1 0 0 0 setv cls2 2 1 156 setv attr 16 mvto 5000 1330 tick 20 slow
scrp 2 1 156 9
* (all in one tick: without INST a C2 script runs 5 steps a tick, and this
* pass over every object took tens of seconds, so creatures waited in the
* pit for it; owner, 2026-11-14, "creatures get stuck here")
  inst
  enum 2 0 0
    setv var0 attr
    andv var0 1
    doif var0 eq 1 and posl gt 2308 and posx lt 3060 and posb gt 2300 and posb lt 2420
      setv var1 posb
      subv var1 post
      setv var2 2320
      subv var2 var1
      subv var2 1
      rndv var3 1900 2150
      mvto var3 var2
      setv velx 0
      setv vely 0
    endi
  next
  enum 4 0 0
    setv var0 0
    doif posx gt 2206 and posx lt 2800 and posb gt 2350 and posb lt 2420
      setv var0 1
    endi
    doif posl gt 2330 and posx lt 2800 and posb gt 2190 and posb lt 2420
      setv var0 1
    endi
    doif posx ge 2800 and posx lt 3060 and posb gt 2190 and posb lt 2420
      setv var0 1
    endi
    doif var0 eq 1 and ov90 eq 0
*     a carrier of its own (2 1 158), so creatures arriving together are
*     carried at once rather than waiting their turn on the ramp; OV90 = 1
*     marks one being carried
      setv ov90 1
      setv var8 targ
      new: simp blnk 1 0 0 0 setv cls2 2 1 158 setv attr 16 setv ov00 var8 mvto 5000 1330 tick 1
      targ var8
    endi
  next
endm
* The carrier: takes its creature (OV00) along, then is removed.
scrp 2 1 158 9
* The ride is not perfectly smooth (owner, 2026-11-15: "the slightest of
* jerkiness ... not perfectly smooth, which comes off as unnatural"): the
* straight runs vary their speed a little each tick (planks 4-8 px, bed
* 11-17, back west 8-12), and about one step in eight (all four parts,
* the rim too) holds an extra tick, a small hitch. VAR9 is the dice.
  tick 0
* (each step INST: WAIT ends INST, and at 5 steps a tick each move took
* about 5 ticks, which made the carrying jerky)
  inst
  targ ov00
*     var1 the middle's x, var2 half the width, var3 the height
  setv var1 posx
  setv var2 posr
  subv var2 posl
  divv var2 2
  setv var3 post
  negv var3
  addv var3 posb
*     on the planks: down them first, 6 px a tick, its feet on their slope
*     (y 2320 to x 2332, then 0.3 px down per px east), to the bed
  setv var5 posb
  doif var5 lt 2372 and var1 lt 2545
    loop
      rndv var9 4 8
      addv var1 var9
      setv var4 var1
      subv var4 var2
      setv var5 var1
      subv var5 2332
      mulv var5 30
      divv var5 100
      addv var5 2320
      doif var5 lt 2320
        setv var5 2320
      endi
      setv var7 var5
      subv var7 var3
      mvto var4 var7
      wait 1
      inst
      rndv var9 0 7
      doif var9 eq 0
        setv vely 0
        wait 1
        inst
      endi
    untl var5 ge 2378
  endi
*     along the bed, 14 px a tick, to below the wheel's hub (x 2947; the
*     pit's floor rises from x 2900, so the feet do too); the rock's own
*     foreground picture (x 2594-2987) and then the wheel hide it. One caught
*     east of the hub (on the pit's rising floor) slides back west to it.
*     VELY is zeroed each step so gravity does not build up while carried.
  doif var1 lt 2947
    loop
      rndv var9 11 17
      addv var1 var9
      doif var1 gt 2947 setv var1 2947 endi
      setv var4 var1
      subv var4 var2
      setv var5 2380
      doif var1 gt 2900
        setv var7 var1
        subv var7 2900
        mulv var7 2
        divv var7 3
        subv var5 var7
      endi
      subv var5 var3
      mvto var4 var5
      setv vely 0
      wait 1
      inst
      rndv var9 0 7
      doif var9 eq 0
        setv vely 0
        wait 1
        inst
      endi
    untl var1 ge 2947
  else
    loop
      rndv var9 8 12
      subv var1 var9
      doif var1 lt 2947 setv var1 2947 endi
      setv var4 var1
      subv var4 var2
      setv var7 var1
      subv var7 2900
      mulv var7 2
      divv var7 3
      setv var5 2380
      subv var5 var7
      subv var5 var3
      mvto var4 var5
      setv vely 0
      wait 1
      inst
      rndv var9 0 7
      doif var9 eq 0
        setv vely 0
        wait 1
        inst
      endi
    untl var1 le 2947
  endi
*     round the wheel's rim as it turns (owner, 2026-11-14: "follow the
*     contour of the waterwheel ... a circular movement"): the wheel is drawn
*     as a tall ellipse (x 2873-3021, y 2100-2392) turning with the stream,
*     its foot moving east, its east side rising, its top moving west. The
*     creature's feet ride an ellipse about (2947, 2249), 64 wide and 100
*     high each way, from its foot (2349, the bed there) up the east side to
*     its top (2149, the walkway's height), half a turn in 30 ticks. Cosine
*     and sine (times 10000, var6 and var7) step 6 degrees a tick by a
*     rotation that keeps their size (C2's CAOS has no trigonometry).
  setv var6 0
  setv var7 10000
  reps 30
    setv var0 var7
    mulv var0 1047
    divv var0 10000
    addv var6 var0
    setv var0 var6
    mulv var0 1047
    divv var0 10000
    subv var7 var0
    setv var1 var6
    mulv var1 64
    divv var1 10000
    addv var1 2947
    setv var4 var1
    subv var4 var2
    setv var5 var7
    mulv var5 100
    divv var5 10000
    addv var5 2249
    subv var5 var3
    mvto var4 var5
    setv vely 0
    wait 1
    inst
    rndv var9 0 7
    doif var9 eq 0
      setv vely 0
      wait 1
      inst
    endi
  repe
*     and set down on the ledge, a short step west from the wheel's top,
*     its feet just above the floor; from there it goes where it likes
*     (owner, 2026-11-14: "deliver them to the cliff where the bridge
*     starts ... at the top of the waterwheel")
  setv var4 2947
  subv var4 var2
  setv var5 2148
  subv var5 var3
  reps 6
    subv var4 9
    mvto var4 var5
    setv vely 0
    wait 1
    inst
    rndv var9 0 7
    doif var9 eq 0
      setv vely 0
      wait 1
      inst
    endi
  repe
  setv vely 1
  setv ov90 0
  targ ownr
  kill ownr
endm
* (after a load, no carriers are left and no creature counts as being carried)
enum 2 1 158 kill targ next
enum 4 0 0 setv ov90 0 next
